/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/ Temporal types (kdb+/q convention). Phase 1: literals, scalars, arithmetic,
/ casts, and the `.qpl.*` now-functions. Column bucketing (`xbar`) and `within`
/ land in Phase 2.
/
/   date       2024.03.15
/   month      2024.03m
/   time       12:30:00.000                      (ms)
/   minute     12:30
/   second     12:30:00
/   timestamp  2024.03.15D12:30:00.000000000     (ns)
/   timespan   0D12:30:00.000000000              (ns duration)
/
/   .qpl.d  today's date         .qpl.p  now (timestamp, ns)
/   .qpl.t  now (time)           .qpl.n  now (timespan since midnight)   -- UTC
/
/ Run from the repo root:
/   cargo run -- examples/temporal.qpl
/ ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/ literals bind like any scalar
d:  2024.03.15
p:  2024.03.15D09:30:00.000000000
n:  0D00:05:00.000000000

log "date       " d
log "timestamp  " p
log "timespan   " n

/ arithmetic — days on a date, a nanosecond offset on a timestamp
log "d + 10     " d + 10                     / 2024.03.25
log "p - 5 min  " p - n                      / 2024.03.15D09:25:00.000000000
log "span days  " 2024.03.20 - 2024.03.15    / 5

/ comparison (temporals order by their underlying offset)
log "before?    " p < 2024.03.15D16:00:00.0  / 1b

/ casts: `` `date$ ``, `` `month$ ``, `` `timestamp$ ``, and the kdb type codes
log "ts->date   " `date$p                    / 2024.03.15
log "date->mon  " `month$d                    / 2024.03m
log "date->ts   " `timestamp$d                / 2024.03.15D00:00:00.000000000
log "raw days   " `int$d                      / 8840   (days since 2000.01.01)
log "parsed     " "p"$"2024.06.01D12:00:00"   / 2024.06.01D12:00:00.000000000

/ now-functions work in queries too (here just as scalars)
log "today      " .qpl.d

/ temporal literals project as Polars-native typed columns
trades: load `examples/data/trades.parquet
select sym, asof: 2024.03.15D09:30:00.000000000 from trades
